[center][size=6][b][color=#f5c542]Pinned Challenges[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][i]Pin the challenges you're chasing and watch their progress during the run.[/i][/size]

[size=2]Version 1.0.0 · The Spell Brigade 1.1.4 · MelonLoader 0.7[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Pin from the Challenges menu[/b] — click a challenge card: the pin in its corner turns gold. Up to 3 at a time by default (1–5 in the settings); pinning one more replaces the oldest.
[*][b]See them during the run[/b] — compact cards with the challenge icon, its description in your language, a progress bar and a live counter like [b]366 / 1 066[/b].
[*][b]Done is done[/b] — a completed challenge turns gold and is unpinned by the next run.
[*][b]Out of the way[/b] — the cards hide while the upgrade screen is open and come back after your pick.
[*][b]Put them anywhere[/b] — drag the cards with the mouse, resize them with the wheel or the corner handle. Saved as a share of the screen, so it fits any resolution.
[*][b]Your look[/b] — card size, game-style or plain background, background opacity and text opacity separately.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/LavaGang/MelonLoader/releases]MelonLoader[/url] (0.7.x) for The Spell Brigade and launch the game once.
[*]Put [b]PinnedChallenges.dll[/b] into [font=Courier New]<Game folder>\Mods\[/font]
[*]Open the Challenges menu, click the cards you want, start a run.
[/list]

[b]Settings[/b] live in [url=https://github.com/Everelsu/SpellBrigade/tree/main/ModMenu]Mod Menu[/url] ([b]Options → Mods → Pinned Challenges[/b]): card size, background, text opacity, how many can be pinned, [b]Card position[/b] (the drag-and-drop editor) and [b]Unpin all[/b]. Mod Menu is optional — without it, the same values are in [font=Courier New]UserData\MelonPreferences.cfg[/font].

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Does it work in co-op?[/b]
Yes. Challenges are yours alone, so the cards show your own progress; other players don't need the mod.

[b]Can I pin with a controller?[/b]
Pinning is a click on the card, so it needs a mouse for now. [b]Unpin all[/b] in Mod Menu works with a controller.

[b]How do I uninstall?[/b]
Delete [b]PinnedChallenges.dll[/b] from the Mods folder.

[line]

